want to just summarize the pros and cons
of sub agents one more time. So, when

00:10:05.839 --> 00:10:13.920
you're thinking about using sub agents
as the way to add functionality versus

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:18.079
things like skills and commands,
remember first of all it allows you to

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:22.320
do more in parallel at the same time.
You can have multiple sub agents working

00:10:19.839 --> 00:10:25.360
together. They can be self-corrective.
They can they can not only allow you to

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:28.880
do more at once, but they can also sort
of have a negative feedback that they

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:32.959
keep you more under control doing a bit
less. They can be very efficient for

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:37.279
your context. It's usually the first
reason you use sub agents is because you

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:41.680
pull stuff off the main context for
clawed code and they can be focused on

00:10:39.519 --> 00:10:46.800
one task that allows you to to perfect
the prompting, perfect the task at hand,

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:51.600
do one thing really well and and be
really good at it, keeping again that

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:56.959
kind of context off your main clawed
code. But with these strengths come a

00:10:54.320 --> 00:11:01.519
few drawbacks. So anytime you've got
this kind of uh ability to delegate to

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:05.760
some other process, you're adding more
moving parts, there's more complexity in

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:10.480
your system, which means that more
things can go wrong in a mysterious way

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:14.959
that's harder to track down. There are
what I call boundary issues or problems

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:19.440
at the at the interfaces between your
sub agent and your your main agent that

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:24.160
can result in mistakes. You can have
this this amplification of problems when

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:27.600
you divvy up the task. something can go
a bit wrong and then agents go off in

00:11:26.079 --> 00:11:32.880
different directions and it gets more
and more wrong in a way that's kind of

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:37.120
hard to recover. Compounding errors and
then also whilst sub agents are

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:41.440
sometimes touted as a way to save money
because you can use a cheaper model to

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:45.360
do to do some of your processing they
can also be a way that money can add up

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:48.640
because you're just doing a lot more. or
you've got more churn, particularly if

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:52.640
you've got the sort of self-correcting
agents that are doing code reviews,

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:56.240
doing document reviews, coming back for
